### Toddle Compose rtc-server — full API test suite
#
# How to run:
#   - JetBrains IDEs (WebStorm/IntelliJ): open this file, pick the "dev" env in the
#     top-right dropdown, then click the green ▶ gutter icon per request.
#   - VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request".
#
# Prereqs:
#   1. RTC Postgres up + schema applied:
#        pnpm --filter @app/rtc-server exec prisma db push   # (or the package's db:push script)
#   2. rtc-server running:  pnpm --filter rtc-server dev   (HTTP + WS on :4001)
#
# Auth model:
#   - GET /health is open.
#   - Everything under /internal/docs is guarded by the InternalTokenGuard — send the
#     shared secret in the `X-Internal-Token` header ({{internalToken}}, default
#     "dev-internal-secret-change-me" in dev). These are server-to-server endpoints the
#     backend calls; they are NOT exposed to browsers.
#   - The collaborative editing transport is a WebSocket (see the bottom of this file),
#     not HTTP, so it can't be exercised from a .http file.
#
# Set {{docId}} in http-client.env.json to a real document id (created via the backend),
# or run "Ensure an RTC doc exists" below first with a docId of your choosing.

# =============================================================================
# 0. HEALTH  (no auth)
# =============================================================================

### Liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

# =============================================================================
# 1. INTERNAL DOC ADMIN  (/internal/docs)  — X-Internal-Token required
# =============================================================================

### Ensure an RTC doc row exists for this id (idempotent). The backend calls this when
### a document is first opened so the Yjs persistence has somewhere to append updates.
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/init
X-Internal-Token: {{internalToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "docId": "{{docId}}" }

### List a doc's persisted Yjs updates (the raw history rows; newest range bounded by head).
### Optional filters: from / to (seq range), limit (1–5000, default 1000), clientSub (author).
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/{{docId}}/versions?from=1&limit=1000
X-Internal-Token: {{internalToken}}

### Filter the update list to a single author (clientSub = the RTC token subject)
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/{{docId}}/versions?clientSub={{clientSub}}
X-Internal-Token: {{internalToken}}

### Preview the materialized doc state at a given update seq (400 if seq isn't a
### non-negative integer). Used to render read-only history snapshots.
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/{{docId}}/versions/0
X-Internal-Token: {{internalToken}}

### Build per-author edit sessions (history timeline). Optional: clientSub (filter author),
### gapMs (session split threshold), includeNoop (true/1 to keep no-op updates).
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/{{docId}}/sessions
X-Internal-Token: {{internalToken}}

### Sessions for a single author, custom gap, including no-op updates
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/{{docId}}/sessions?clientSub={{clientSub}}&gapMs=120000&includeNoop=true
X-Internal-Token: {{internalToken}}

### Force a checkpoint + compaction pass for a warm doc (demo/diagnostic only).
### tier=1 or tier=2 required (400 otherwise); 409 if the doc isn't warm — open it
### in the editor first so it's live in memory.
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/{{docId}}/compact-demo?tier=1
X-Internal-Token: {{internalToken}}

### Tier-2 compaction variant
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/{{docId}}/compact-demo?tier=2
X-Internal-Token: {{internalToken}}

### Delete a doc completely — tears down any live session (closes sockets) and drops
### the doc + all its update rows. Idempotent. Destructive; run in cleanup.
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/{{docId}}
# X-Internal-Token: {{internalToken}}

### Edge: missing/incorrect internal token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/docs/{{docId}}/versions
X-Internal-Token: wrong-token

# =============================================================================
# 2. COLLABORATIVE TRANSPORT  (WebSocket — not runnable from .http)
# =============================================================================
#
# The Yjs sync + awareness protocol runs over a WebSocket, documented here for reference:
#
#   ws://localhost:4001/yjs/{{docId}}?token=<rtc-jwt>
#
# - The RTC JWT is minted by the backend: POST /api/documents/:id/rtc-token.
# - The token may instead be supplied as a `bearer.<token>` entry in the WS subprotocol
#   list; such clients MUST also offer the `yjs` subprotocol (the only one selected).
# - The token is verified once at connect against the backend JWKS; the socket is closed
#   with 1008 when the token expires.
